  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal obligations to Idaho totaled $126M in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year. The state received 225 awards with an average award size of $561K. The largest single buyer listed for FY2027 to date is the Department of Energy, which obligated $177M. Top vendors in the current fiscal year include BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC with $90.5M and IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC with $83.2M. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services is the largest industry by obligations at $90.5M, followed by Remediation Services at $83.2M. Annual context shows obligations by fiscal year of $2.5B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.8B in FY24, $4B in FY25, $4.3B in FY26, and $126M in FY27. Note that all figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did FY2027 to date compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations to Idaho for FY2027 to date were $126M. Obligations fell 97.0% year over year. Fiscal-year context shows prior-year totals of $2.5B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.8B in FY24, $4B in FY25, and $4.3B in FY26. The FY2027 total is a partial, fiscal year to date number."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest agencies, vendors, and industries in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the largest buying agency with $177M obligated. Top vendors are BATTELLE ENERGY ALLIANCE, LLC with $90.5M and IDAHO ENVIRONMENTAL COALITION LLC with $83.2M. Leading industries are All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $90.5M and Remediation Services at $83.2M."
      }
    ]
